"""
Templates of Hilde's Jinja dialect for tenants, read from directories
while the programme runs and rendered with a Wolly.ViewData: the run-time
counterpart of @template, with the same syntax, the same refusals and the
same escaping.

An engine holds a list of directories, the tenant's first and the shared
one after it, and looks for a name in each in turn; the functions a
template may call and the catalogs it may translate with; and the
templates it has loaded.  One engine serves one tenant, so nothing it
keeps is another tenant's.

Loading checks the whole template, and everything it extends, includes
and imports, before anything is rendered: a mistake of the text is an
error with the template's name and line then (Wolly.ViewCompile).  What
only the data can tell is an error of the render, with the line: a name
the data does not have, a value that cannot be printed (a list, a map, a
missing value not asked with is none), a number where a text is asked,
HTML outside HTML text.  Every error is a Left; nothing a template does
stops the programme, and out gets a page only when it rendered whole.

A loaded template is kept.  Standard.Watch reports a change of a file
read or of a directory searched, and the next render drops all that was
kept.  Where watching is not built, nothing is kept.

A function is Fn[ViewData, Either[String, ViewData]]: its arguments come
as a list, its result is the root of what it gives back, and a Left is an
error of the render.  A catalog is the same kind of function, given a map
with lang, key, count and arguments; it gives back the text.

The limits of a render: mostLoopTurns turns of all loops, mostMadeBytes
bytes of text made (kept or not), mostMadeNodes nodes given to functions
and given back, mostComparedBytes bytes searched by in and |replace (the
text and the part, since both search in linear time),
mostOutputBytes
bytes written.
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Standard.StringBuilder (
    StringBuilder
);
import Wolly.ViewData (
    ViewData
);

module Wolly.View is
    """
    A template engine.  Linear: destroyViewEngine gives it back.
    """
    type ViewEngine: Linear;

    """
    The limits of a render: 1000000 turns of all loops together, 16 MiB
    written.
    """
    function mostLoopTurns(): Index
        ensures result = 1000000;
    function mostOutputBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 16777216;
    function mostMadeBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 67108864;
    function mostMadeNodes(): Index
        ensures result = 4194304;
    function mostComparedBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 67108864;

    """
    An engine without directories, functions or catalogs, with the
    whitespace options off.
    """
    function makeViewEngine(): ViewEngine
        ensures directoryCount(&result) = 0;

    """
    Gives the engine and all it keeps back.
    No contract: nothing is left to ask.
    """
    function destroyViewEngine(engine: ViewEngine): Unit;

    """
    One more directory, searched after those added before.  What was kept
    is dropped: a name may now be found elsewhere.
    """
    generic [R: Region, D: Region]
    function addDirectory(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], directory: Span[Nat8, D]): Unit
        ensures directoryCount(&engine) = (old(directoryCount(&engine)) + 1)
        ensures keptViews(&engine) = 0;

    """
    How many directories the engine searches.
    No contract: any number.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function directoryCount(engine: &[ViewEngine, R]): Index;

    """
    A function a template may call by name; a name given twice keeps the
    first.  What was kept is dropped, unless the name was given before.
    No contract: which of the two happened is not asked cheaply.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function addFunction(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], name: Span[Nat8, N], callable: Fn[ViewData, Either[String, ViewData]]): Unit;

    """
    A catalog a template may name with {% catalog name %}.  What was kept is
    dropped, unless the name was given before.
    No contract: as addFunction.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function addCatalog(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], name: Span[Nat8, N], catalog: Fn[ViewData, Either[String, ViewData]]): Unit;

    """
    Jinja2's options trim_blocks and lstrip_blocks, for every template the
    engine loads from now on.  What was kept is dropped.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function setWhitespace(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], trimBlocks: Bool, lstripBlocks: Bool): Unit
        ensures keptViews(&engine) = 0;

    """
    The template name loaded and checked, and kept; Left with the first
    mistake.
    No contract: it reads files.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region]
    function loadView(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], name: Span[Nat8, N]): Either[String, Unit];

    """
    The template name rendered with data into out.  Left with the first
    error, of the load or of the render, and nothing written to out then.
    No contract: it reads files.
    """
    generic [R: Region, N: Region, D: Region, B: Region]
    function renderView(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], name: Span[Nat8, N], data: &[ViewData, D],
        out: &![StringBuilder, B]): Either[String, Unit];

    """
    The page rendered inside the layout, as the Go templates the view
    replaces render a page: the page loaded as if {% extends layout %} stood at its head, so that its
    blocks fill the layout's.  As renderView otherwise.
    No contract: it reads files.
    """
    generic [R: Region, P: Region, L: Region, D: Region, B: Region]
    function renderPage(engine: &![ViewEngine, R], page: Span[Nat8, P], layout: Span[Nat8, L], data: &[ViewData, D],
        out: &![StringBuilder, B]): Either[String, Unit];

    """
    How many templates the engine keeps loaded.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function keptViews(engine: &[ViewEngine, R]): Index
        ensures keepsViews(engine) or (result = 0);

    """
    Whether the engine keeps what it loads: where Standard.Watch is built.
    A template whose files cannot all be watched is not kept even then.
    No contract: a truth of the platform.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function keepsViews(engine: &[ViewEngine, R]): Bool;
end module.
